WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.884
Module 6: the practical.

00:00:01.884 --> 00:00:03.925
This is where you show us.

00:00:03.925 --> 00:00:08.165
You'll build a real survey
to a client brief, test it,

00:00:08.165 --> 00:00:11.069
and explain your choices on one page.

00:00:11.069 --> 00:00:14.838
Most people need two to
three hours to build it.

00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:16.847
Here's how it works.

00:00:16.847 --> 00:00:17.982
Read the brief.

00:00:17.982 --> 00:00:22.824
Design the survey on paper first:
objectives, questions, scales,

00:00:22.824 --> 00:00:24.565
demographics and logic.

00:00:24.565 --> 00:00:27.213
Build it in the practice workspace.

00:00:27.213 --> 00:00:31.829
Test it: walk every path in
Preview, generate test responses,

00:00:31.829 --> 00:00:37.504
check their rows on the Responses page,
and then delete the test responses.

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:41.514
Publish it so the assessor
can take it from the link,

00:00:41.514 --> 00:00:44.011
but don't send it to anyone else.

00:00:44.011 --> 00:00:50.367
Write your one-page rationale, put it in
one file with your screenshots, and submit.

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:53.394
You get one resubmission if you need it.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.842
In August, Jordan Reyes published
a decision-rights charter.

00:00:57.842 --> 00:01:02.507
Alex wants a short check before the
Progress Monitor starts in October.

00:01:02.507 --> 00:01:04.740
Do people know the charter exists?

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:07.500
Do they understand what it means for them?

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.836
And do they feel more involved in
decisions than they did in June?

00:01:11.836 --> 00:01:13.741
Read the constraints closely.

00:01:13.741 --> 00:01:17.815
Five hundred and twenty-seven
people across three departments,

00:01:17.815 --> 00:01:20.574
a hundred and fifty of them without email.

00:01:20.574 --> 00:01:22.479
Spanish for Support Services.

00:01:22.479 --> 00:01:25.239
Ten questions at most, under five minutes.

00:01:25.239 --> 00:01:27.604
June's decision item, word for word.

00:01:27.604 --> 00:01:30.823
And Taylor will ask for
clinic-by-clinic results.

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.188
Your design has to handle all of it.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.978
You'll submit three things: the
survey's link, its exact name,

00:01:37.978 --> 00:01:43.360
and one file with your one-page rationale
and your screenshots: the test rows,

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:46.396
Preview on each path,
and the settings page.

00:01:46.396 --> 00:01:49.638
The survey must be
anonymous, tested and clean,

00:01:49.638 --> 00:01:52.743
with a future close date
and Spanish offered.

00:01:53.233 --> 00:01:56.216
Use this template for your rationale.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:02:02.828
Eight short sections: decision and objectives,
a question map, scales and wording,

00:02:02.828 --> 00:02:08.794
logic and testing, confidentiality,
distribution and reminders, languages,

00:02:08.794 --> 00:02:10.729
and your reporting plan.

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:11.455
One page.

00:02:11.455 --> 00:02:12.825
Clear beats long.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:13.544
Dr.

00:02:13.544 --> 00:02:18.607
Chris Cancialosi scores six criteria
from one to four: fit to the brief,

00:02:18.607 --> 00:02:23.670
item and scale quality, logic and
testing, confidentiality and settings,

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:28.030
your distribution plan, and your
rationale and reporting plan.

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:30.561
You need three or more on every one.

00:02:30.561 --> 00:02:33.304
Four things fail a submission outright,

00:02:33.304 --> 00:02:38.085
whatever the scores: promising
anonymity the settings don't deliver,

00:02:38.085 --> 00:02:43.429
a design or reporting plan that would
report a group below the minimum size,

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:48.703
test responses left in the survey, and
copying a bought instrument's items.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.744
Before you submit, run the self-check.

00:02:51.744 --> 00:02:56.296
Pay special attention to three items:
June's question word for word,

00:02:56.296 --> 00:03:01.450
no clinic-by-clinic results, and
screenshots taken before you delete the test

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:02.119
responses.

00:03:02.119 --> 00:03:04.194
Those are the ones people miss.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:08.408
You can take the final exam
before or after the practical.

00:03:08.408 --> 00:03:11.540
Thirty questions, forty-five
minutes, open notes.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.992
You need eighty percent and
every critical item right.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.862
Build to the brief.

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:20.231
Make the promise true
and protect small groups.

00:03:20.231 --> 00:03:21.665
Test, then clean up.

00:03:21.665 --> 00:03:23.170
Explain your choices.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:27.113
Do that, and you're a certified
SurveyCraft Specialist.

00:03:27.113 --> 00:03:27.830
Good luck.

